776:At shorter contexts, the selection of the keys costs more than it saves.
777:Its peak memory is higher, at 6.8 GiB against 5.8 GiB per layer at 128k tokens, partly because N-LSA keeps the indices of the selected keys of every query for the backward pass, which grow linearly with the context. 
778: Overall, N-LSA trains natively at the accuracy of Full Attention and becomes faster as the context grows. 
780: LSA reduces the cost of finding the keys, but not of storing them, and the KV cache still grows linearly with the context.
781:It is orthogonal to methods that compress the KV cache  ( DeepSeek-AI, 2026a ) , share the index across layers  ( Bai et al., 2026 ; DeepSeek-AI, 2026b ) , or predict several tokens per step  ( Gloeckle et al., 2024 ; DeepSeek-AI, 2024 ) , and could be combined with each. 
782: We observed tree search to lose accuracy faster than flat search past 1M tokens on GLM-5.3-Flash , while it overtakes flat search in decode only from about 5M tokens with one request, and is predicted to do so in prefill only beyond 10M tokens.
784: We train N-LSA at a small scale, with about 0.5B parameters, up to 128k tokens and with flat search only.
785:Scaling native training to larger models, longer contexts and tree search remains open. 
787: At ultra-long context, the cost of sparse attention lies in finding which keys to attend to.
789:D-LSA distils LSA into pre-trained models and stays close to the accuracy of their baseline attention up to 10M tokens.
790:At 10M tokens, one attention layer of D-LSA prefills 22.7 × \times and decodes 4.6 × \times faster than sparse attention in GLM-5.3-Flash , and 72.4 × \times and 42.5 × \times faster than Full Attention in Qwen-3.8-27B .
791:End to end, this reduces the time to first token by 2.2 × \times and 9.2 × \times , respectively.
792:N-LSA trains LSA natively on the next-token loss alone, at the accuracy of Full Attention and 1.6 × \times faster per layer at 128k tokens.
793:With tree search, the cost of finding the keys grows subquadratically, which makes LSA a step towards attention that scales well beyond 10M tokens.
794:LSA thus provides a practical way forward for ultra-long context attention, both for distilling pre-trained models and for native training. 
