# Qwen3.8-27B, the dense-attention model LSA is carried to after GLM-5.3-Flash. 64 layers - 48 Gated DeltaNet
# and 16 full attention, every fourth - GQA of 24 query heads on 4 key-value heads of 256 dims, 64 of them
# rotated, and 262,144 tokens native.
#
# The model is frozen and served with YaRN to 10M, so it is distilled under the same rotation: an index map is
# trained on the q, k and attention it is later served with. `rope_parameters` is that one setting, merged
# over the checkpoint's own at load by every harness that reads this card - the teacher extraction, the
# online teacher in distillation and the server, which passes it as `--json-model-override-args`.
# A factor of 40 on the native 262,144 is 10,485,760 positions, the shortest round factor past a 10M prompt
# and its answer. The rest is the checkpoint's own block, which the override replaces whole.
#
# `output_gate_type: swish` in its config is the Gated DeltaNet norm's activation, which transformers already
# applies as silu; the full-attention output gate is a sigmoid either way.

name: qwen38_27b
about: Qwen3.8-27B - the dense-attention model, served and distilled with YaRN to 10M
repo: Qwen/Qwen3.8-27b
revision: 1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0
family: qwen3_5
flavor: 27B
rotary_end: prefix
rotary_dim: 64
rope_parameters:
  mrope_interleaved: true
  mrope_section: [11, 11, 10]
  rope_type: yarn
  rope_theta: 10000000
  partial_rotary_factor: 0.25
  factor: 40.0
  original_max_position_embeddings: 262144
attention: full
===
# `full` takes every shape from the published config. The two narrowed flavours a run names instead are
# `debugmodel`, which keeps the first four layers and narrows the experts 288 to 32, and `first_layers`,
# which keeps the first four at every published width so published weights can be read into them
flavor: full

# Left unset on purpose, each for its own reason:
#
# path:         only a checkpoint this repository wrote has one - a published snapshot is read by revision
# adapter:      the harness resolves its own driver from the checkpoint's `model_type`, and naming one here
#               would pin a choice this model has never been served through
# layer_types:  only needed when the quadratic layers LSA replaces are called something other than
#               `full_attention`; GLM's are `deepseek_sparse_attention` and the trainer reads that from the
#               config rather than from here
# rotary_end:   GLM's quadratic layers are MLA with `qk_rope_head_dim` 0, so nothing rotates and the index
# rotary_dim: space is the whole head - but this repository has not measured that through the harness, and
#               a pin that is wrong raises where no pin merely measures. Pinned once it is measured
#
# Not here at all, and deliberately: whether the embedding is tied, and whether the weights are fp8. Both
# are read off the snapshot's own `config.json` at load, because a flag set by hand for every checkpoint
# will be wrong for one of them - which is exactly what happened to Qwen3.5, where the registry said no
# flavour ties and the published 4B does.
# DSA - a learned indexer of its own, which `native` serves
attention: block_sparse
