 Appendix A Attention Sparsity 
 To test how many keys a query needs to keep accuracy, we let each query of Qwen-3.8-27B attend only to the sink, the window and its true top- k k keys (Figure  8 ).
At 128k tokens, Top- k k Oracle Attention keeps 98% of the RULER accuracy of Full Attention down to k = 512 k=512 , while each query attends to 0.8% of the keys.
Single-needle retrieval holds down to k = 16 k=16 , while MultiKey 2, MultiKey 3 and CWE fall first in accuracy.
Therefore, sparse attention loses little if it finds the most relevant keys, which is what LSA is designed to do without scoring every key. 
