 E.6 Block Size 
 Figure 14: Block size of Block Sparse Attention (Tree). 
RULER and PaperTrail up to 1M tokens with blocks of 8, 16 and 64 keys ( n pool n_{\mathrm{pool}} ), each selecting the same 4,608 keys, against the baseline of each model and D-LSA (Flat). 
 Figure  14 compares Block Sparse Attention (Tree) with blocks of 8, 16 and 64 keys, all selecting the same number of keys.
At short context, every block size matches the baseline.
As the context grows, accuracy falls earlier and further the larger the block, on both benchmarks and both models, as a larger block summarises more keys in one score and can hide a single relevant key.
Even with blocks of eight keys, the size we use in the main results, the tree baseline trails D-LSA (Flat) at long context. 
